  "root_read_coverage": "Complete candidate, staged addendum, author checker/launcher and full output, and all 515 lines of the separate comparison read; inherited unchanged sources reused by identity. Hash validation is not proof review.",
  "judgment": [
    "Full-space positive-complement identity Hprep=K+cprep I+Haux holds, with Haux>=Delta D and a unique auxiliary seed ground.",
    "All N=M+3 auxiliary qubits and many-head sectors enter the Gibbs estimate through ordered-eigenvalue min-max; no operator monotonicity of exponential or commutation with D is presumed.",
    "The arbitrary-correlated complete-input trace estimate uses the actual unconditioned old/reference marginal and g(epsilon)=epsilon+sqrt(epsilon(4-3epsilon)); smaller product-joint estimates are not silently imported.",
    "Common release pays sqrt(2) kappa tau in trace, actual scalar and full old aging. Staged release holds emitter complements while removing other seed-scalar controls, so the early nominal leakage is exactly zero; only the late emitter ramp incurs kappa tau_e/sqrt(2) in isometry.",
    "Finite-slew nonempty early stages require D>0; V_seed is a scaled isometry with Gram 2I. These clarify frozen wording without altering its formulas or D=10000 example.",
    "Every modeled qubit/reference output is retained, but prescribed controls and delivered thermal marginal remain external conditional supplies. Physical isolation, calibration, native Hamiltonian, cooling and reset/reuse are open.",
    "Positive controls imply signed release work nonpositive; extensive identity coefficients and block loads remain paid. This is not a closed cooling/controller-energy or recovered work cycle."
  ],
